  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia Regional Migration Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asia Regional Migration Program (RMP) aims to strengthen governments&#x2019; and key national stakeholders&#x2019; ability to manage migration in a safe, sustainable, and humane manner. Asia RMP targets programming in 12 countries in Southeast Asia (Cambodia, Indonesia, Lao People&#x2019;s Democratic Republic, Malaysia, Myanmar, Thailand, and Viet Nam), South Asia (Bangladesh) and Central Asia (Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan, and Tajikistan), including interventions implemented regionally. The proposed activities build upon the development gains and progress from previous phases of the Asia RMP. The interventions proposed have been designed in coordination with target governments and counterparts and appropriately respond to gaps and needs identified through formal assessments and ongoing project activities in Central, South, and Southeast Asia. The program has been strategically conceptualized to serve and respond to a framework of three common outcome areas: (I) migration management; (II) partnerships; and (III) crisis response.</narrative>
  </description>
